# Create /opt/farmos/mosquitto/acl from this file and replace each example user
# with a unique, non-human credential. Do not grant '#' or '+/#' to gateways.

user farmos-backend
topic read farm/+/node/+/telemetry
topic read farm/+/node/+/status
topic read farm/+/node/+/ack
topic write farm/+/zone/+/command

# Example: a gateway may read only its farm's commands and write only status/ACK
# for itself plus telemetry from the sensor nodes physically assigned to it.
# Copy the block with a unique username per gateway and enumerate every assigned
# sensor node. Do not use a `+` wildcard for node IDs: it would let one gateway
# impersonate another node in the same farm.
# user gateway-f01-01
# topic read farm/F01/zone/+/command
# topic write farm/F01/node/GATEWAY_01/status
# topic write farm/F01/node/GATEWAY_01/ack
# topic write farm/F01/node/NODE_Z01_01/telemetry
# topic write farm/F01/node/NODE_Z02_01/telemetry
# topic write farm/F01/node/NODE_Z03_01/telemetry
